  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Universal Green Energy Access Programme (UGEAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme is an investment fund designed to mobilize private sector funding through on-lending to local financial institutions and syndicated loans for sustainable energy access in sub-Saharan Africa.

&#x2022; It targets sustainable energy for all in low-income countries in sub-Saharan Africa. The business model of the target investees for customer ownership of solar home systems is expected to empower people, especially women, thereby accelerating local democratization processes and contribute to low-income rural populations.
&#x2022; It enhances local financial institutions&#x2019; knowledge of and appetite for the renewable energy sector
&#x2022; It crowds-in foreign and local private investors into the field of sustainable energy access in sub-Saharan Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
